Good instincts.  Burdened is very bad.

But there's no reason you can't find a chest and stash all your goodies
in it, coming back if you need things.  And maybe some magical
containers would be handy if you could find them, or getting yourself
stronger/tougher.

Also, some loot isn't that important; things that are really common can
be left laying around.  Especially heavy things; no sense dragging 5-6
iron skull caps around with you.  Even that extra suit of plate mail
may be uncommon but not worth dragging around.  I rarely wear very
heavy armor--I try to find some studded leather early, switch it for
dwarven or elvish mithril as soon as possible, and wear that until I
get the good stuff (spoiler below).

So: leave common stuff behind.  Stash uncommon stuff in a central
location if it's worthwile (you might periodically move your stash to
more convenient places).  Excercise and otherwise get yourself strong
(spoilers below), and if you find a magical container then maximize
it's capabilities (spoilers below).

